    <briefdescription>
<para>IR Values for the lower and upper bounds of a pointer evolution. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>We need to use value-handles because <ref refid="classllvm_1_1_s_c_e_v" kindref="compound">SCEV</ref> expansion can invalidate previously expanded values. Thus expansion of a pointer can invalidate the bounds for a previous one. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
